# Project Structure Rules

Before creating any file, determine the correct folder. Create missing folders automatically. Never add unrelated files to the project root.

## Folder Map

| Code type | Location |
|-----------|----------|
| React components (reusable) | `src/components/{common,layout,forms,ui}/` |
| Page views | `src/pages/{PageName}/{PageName}.jsx` |
| Firebase init & API | `src/services/` |
| Custom hooks | `src/hooks/` |
| React context | `src/context/` |
| Routing | `src/routes/` |
| Helpers | `src/utils/` |
| App constants | `src/constants/` |
| Env & config | `src/config/` |
| Type definitions | `src/types/` |
| CSS | `src/assets/styles/` |
| Images | `src/assets/images/` |
| Icons | `src/assets/icons/` |
| Static assets | `public/` |
| Firestore rules & schemas | `database/` |
| Seed/cleanup scripts | `scripts/` |
| Documentation | `docs/` |
| Tests | `tests/` |
| CI workflows | `.github/workflows/` |
| Legacy vanilla app | `legacy/` (reference only) |

## Examples

```
# ✅ New login form component
src/components/forms/LoginForm.jsx

# ✅ Resident requests feature
src/pages/Resident/RequestsPanel.jsx

# ✅ Firebase auth helper
src/services/authService.js

# ❌ Never do this
./NewFeature.jsx
./utils.js
```

## New Feature Workflow

1. Identify the feature domain (auth, resident, wdc, admin, etc.)
2. Create the page folder under `src/pages/` if it does not exist
3. Extract reusable UI into `src/components/`
4. Put Firebase calls in `src/services/`
5. Wire routes in `src/routes/AppRoutes.jsx`
